{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTg1MzE2","is_bot":false,"login":"tapios","name":"Tapio Schneider"},"baseRefOid":"2d43bf4c1e40e4fff6085dcb0de6ace627375094","body":"Fixes two problems at the upper boundary and with tracer-mass consistency\r\n* Ensures zero mass flux through top boundary even in the presence of warped coordinate surfaces (before the flux would only be zero if top layers are level)\r\n* Ensures tracer-mass consistency in EDMF by treating all tracers (e.g., condensates) like `mse` and `q_tot`, in difference form, with corresponding Jacobian updates. Reduces SGS mass-flux tendency with an artificially uniform `q_lcl` from 1.1e-7 to 6.7e-14 (Float32 roundoff). \r\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-06T20:43:27Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTg1MzE2","login":"tapios","name":"Tapio Schneider"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-06T20:43:27Z","messageBody":"Over sloped terrain-following coordinates (g³ʰ ≠ 0 at the lid, e.g. with\nLinear mesh warping), ᶠwinterp's Extrapolate top BC copies the topmost\ncell-center uₕ³ to the top face, so zeroing only the covariant u₃ left\nᶠu³ = ᶠuₕ³ ≠ 0 there, and the continuity equation (which used the\nunrestricted ᶜdivᵥ while all tracers use ᶜadvdivᵥ) consumed that flux as\na spurious mass leak through the lid.\n\nMirror the surface treatment at the top: set_velocity_at_top! now takes\nᶠuₕ³ and sets top_u₃ = -uₕ³/g³³ (new top_velocity helper, analogous to\nsurface_velocity), so the total contravariant flux vanishes exactly at\nthe lid. Since all EDMFX subdomain velocities are built from the same\ngrid-mean uₕ and ᶠuₕ³, copying top_u₃ into each u₃ʲ keeps ᶠu³ʲ = 0 too.\n\nIndependently, switch the continuity equation to ᶜadvdivᵥ so the zero\nboundary flux is structural rather than dependent on the state filter,\nrestoring the χ ≡ 1 tracer-mass identity at the boundary rows and making\nthe ρ-row Jacobian (already built from ᶜadvdivᵥ_matrix) exact.\n\nA regression test in advection_tests.jl asserts that ᶠu³ vanishes at\nboth boundary faces over a Schar mountain with Linear warping, where\nᶠuₕ³ ≠ 0 at the lid.\n\nValidated on a Schar-mountain plane with Linear warping: top-face u³\ndrops from 6.5e-6 to machine zero and the total-mass drift from\n-7.8e-13 per 10 steps to exactly 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Enforce u³ = 0 at the model top and zero-flux continuity boundaries","oid":"a77a0a0bd4d2f0bc89a2760900173b4711c09211"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-06T18:21:11Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTg1MzE2","login":"tapios","name":"Tapio Schneider"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-06T20:44:52Z","messageBody":"…flux\n\nTransport the auto-discovered SGS tracers (q_lcl, q_icl, q_rai, q_sno,\nn_*) the same way as mse and q_tot: grid-mean vertical advection (now\napplied unconditionally in explicit_vertical_advection_tendency!) plus\ndifference-form SGS corrections ρᵏaᵏ(u³ᵏ - u³)(χᵏ - χ), which vanish\nidentically for uniform χ. Previously these tracers were transported by\nabsolute subdomain fluxes Σₖ ρᵏaᵏ u³ᵏ χᵏ that replaced the grid-mean\nadvection entirely; the discrete sum does not telescope to the\ncontinuity flux (upwound area fractions vs centrally interpolated ρ,\nρᵏ ≠ ρ, and regularized u₃⁰/χ⁰), producing a spurious source/sink of\neach species where updraft area varies strongly and a drift of the\nwater-species partition relative to q_tot by numerics alone.\n\nUpdate the manual Jacobian tracer blocks to the difference-form\nderivatives: the upwind matrices are built with u³ᵏ - u³; the draft\nloop gains a ∂/∂ρχ entry (-aʲ/ρ); the environment ∂/∂ρχ entry gains\nthe -a⁰/ρ correction; and the ∂/∂u₃ entries use the velocity-difference\nsensitivities (-g³³ for drafts, (ᶠinterp(ρ/ρa⁰) - 1)g³³ for the\nenvironment).\n\nAlso add the moist-air-mass counterpart of the SGS q_tot mass flux:\nYₜ.c.ρ receives the same tendency as Yₜ.c.ρq_tot from both the updraft\nand environment contributions, mirroring the diffusive-flux treatment,\nso vertical SGS redistribution of water also redistributes moist air\nmass term-by-term.\n\nWith a spun-up DYCOMS RF01 EDMFX 1M column, the SGS tendency of a\nuniform tracer drops from ~10% of the q_tot flux scale to roundoff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"EDMFX: difference-form SGS tracer fluxes and ρ counterpart for q_tot …","oid":"aecf5aab5b16eb5a0967b6476794337ab5108ce3"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-06T18:43:13Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTg1MzE2","login":"tapios","name":"Tapio Schneider"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-06T20:44:52Z","messageBody":"The -β·ρq_x damping of the 1M species has no counterpart in ρq_tot, ρ,\nor ρe_tot, so it acts as saturation-blind condensate-to-vapor\nconversion in the sponge layer. Flag it for removal (if unneeded after\nthe top-boundary fixes) or for a mass- and energy-consistent\nreformulation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Add TODO on the grid-mean condensate Rayleigh sponge","oid":"b9ca9a0060f00686a8035018727a1d1fd2414fd5"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-06T20:45:03Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTg1MzE2","login":"tapios","name":"Tapio Schneider"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-06T20:45:03Z","messageBody":"The new test asserts the χ ≡ 1 identity for the fixed transport\npathways: ∂(ρq_x)/∂t = ∂ρ/∂t for uniform tracers through the implicit\nand explicit advection pathways; bitwise equality of the ρ and ρq_tot\ntendencies from the EDMFX SGS mass flux; and vanishing difference-form\nSGS fluxes for uniform tracers. Each